      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of splitting the crate into 2 independent crates (`_std` depending on `_nostd`), crates typically have a `std` feature and hide any part of the implementation relying on `std` behind that feature e.g.\n```\n#![cfg_attr(not(feature \u003d \"std\"), no_std)]\n```\n\nYou could then have 2 flavors of the crate in the (single) Android.bp: `libavb_nostd`(`_rust`) target wouldn\u0027t enable the `std` feature (but would `no_stdlibs: true`) while a non-`_nostd` Soong target would set `std` but not `no_stdlibs`. As long as the interface provided by `_nostd` is a subset of the other one, they can both be export using the common name `avb` (i.e. no need for a separate `avb_nostd`)!",
      "revId": "1eab582b6ae56ad3b9964d7abd8887f4cea31ab9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
